From 428dff0690a19b16883f7479b88fac757822365c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:20:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Honour promoted SUBREG targets in expand_CLMUL

expand_CLMUL stored its result into the call's lhs with emit_move_insn.
When the lhs is a variable kept in a wider register than its mode
(PROMOTE_MODE), the target is a promoted SUBREG and the move writes
only the low part, so the upper bits of the register, which the rest
of the function assumes are zero- or sign-extended, are garbage.

On microblaze-elf, which promotes QImode and HImode to SImode,
c-c++-common/builtin-clmulg-1.c aborts at every optimization level.
Store the result the way the other expanders in this file do, with
convert_move into SUBREG_REG.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* internal-fn.cc (expand_CLMUL): Use convert_move for a promoted
	SUBREG target.
---
 gcc/internal-fn.cc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/internal-fn.cc b/gcc/internal-fn.cc
index 5fc6c3578..e335d8591 100644
--- a/gcc/internal-fn.cc
+++ b/gcc/internal-fn.cc
@@ -6207,7 +6207,10 @@ expand_CLMUL (internal_fn, gcall *stmt)
       res = expand_and (mode, res, mask, NULL_RTX);
     }
   rtx target = expand_expr (lhs, NULL_RTX, VOIDmode, EXPAND_WRITE);
-  emit_move_insn (target, res);
+  if (GET_CODE (target) == SUBREG && SUBREG_PROMOTED_VAR_P (target))
+    convert_move (SUBREG_REG (target), res, SUBREG_PROMOTED_SIGN (target));
+  else
+    emit_move_insn (target, res);
 }
 
 void
